# Response phrasing

- Do not say "you are right", "you're right", or equivalent validation phrasing.
- Use neutral, action-oriented acknowledgements instead.
- Keep acknowledgements short and proceed directly to the fix.

## Examples

- Bad: "You're right. I'll move this logic."
- Good: "Moving this logic into `thought-processing.service.ts` now."
